(home-h2 "My HHKB Experience")

(p
  (italic "Last Updated: 14/08/2026"))

(image "/Images/MyHHKBExperience/MainCompressed.jpg"
  alt: "HHKB Lite2")

(p
  (italic
    (link "/Images/MyHHKBExperience/Main.jpg" "[Original Image]")
    " I actually layered a few images together as just one image would either "
    "blow out the keys in direct sunlight or make the background very dark!"))

(h3 "Overview")

(p
  "This article covers my seven days with my new HHKB Lite2 keyboard. I've "
  "basically \"journaled\" any day I've wanted to update this blog so there may "
  "just be two logs, who knows!")

(p
  "Around a week ago, I ordered a HHKB Lite2 to be imported from Japan. For a long "
  "time, I've wanted a HHKB, but when I checked, they were all ludicrously "
  "expensive. Thats until "
  (link "https://exotya.worthless.love" "my friend")
  " showed me how I could get one for just ~£15 (¥3,200). I bought one shortly "
  "after that.")

(p
  "Now the keyboard isn't a \"proper\" HHKB with the Topre switches and has membrane "
  "instead, but I don't think that really matters as I prefer the sound of "
  "membrane keyboards when programming anyways.")

(p
  "From the image, it looked very yellow (from sun damage) and I assumed that I "
  "would probably want to "
  (link "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Retrobright" "retrobright")
  " it with something like hydrogen-peroxide. It also was a Japanese layout but "
  "all the US layouts were black and all of them were kind of gunky..")

(h3 "Day One: 07/08/2026")

(h4 "Looks")

(p
  "Today I recieved the keyboard (surprisingly, it only took four days after "
  "getting shipped from Japan)! My first impressions were that it's "
  (bold "very")
  " yellow; I initially thought that person who last owned it always had his "
  "curtains open (how brave). It also sounded very pleasing. It was like the "
  "average membrane sound but with a lot more "
  (italic "thock")
  "--overall it was positive.")

(p
  "After a bit of time using it, I noticed that the yellowing was very evenly "
  "coated and actually gave it a very pleasing creamy color. I personally think it "
  "looks even better than the original, greyish colour; I don't think I'll "
  "retrobright it.")

(p
  "I now have a new theory that the keyboard was just propped up on and outfacing "
  "shelf of some store. There isn't a single hair underneath the keycaps and it's "
  "in pristine condition!")

(h4 "Layout")

(p
  "I particularly enjoy the layout on this keyboard. It's basically QWERTY, but "
  "with a few quirks.")

(p
  "The biggest ones are that the CapsLock is CTRL (Caps is now under Tab), there "
  "are four new modifier keys and that it's in a Japanese layout.")

(p
  "While I used to host my ESC key on CapsLock, I think that moving control there "
  "is fine but probably only on this keyboard (see the bit on the four modifiers). "
  "Overall, CTRL with your pinky is very pleasing to use as it's a common key that "
  "I don't have to reach for anymore.")

(p
  "The four extra modifiers for me are useless; I don't know Japanese so they "
  "don't do much. That means I can remap them!")

(table
  (tr
    (th "Key")
    (th "Romanised")
    (th "Remap"))
  (tr
    (td "半角/全角")
    (td (italic "Hankaku/Zenkaku"))
    (td
      (bold "Super")
      " - It was still super but needed Fn to activate. Now it activates without the modifier"))
  (tr
    (td "無変換")
    (td (italic "Muhenkan"))
    (td
      (bold "ESC")
      " - This is where I remapped it to; it's actually much easier to press than CapsLock but I still need to retrain myself"))
  (tr
    (td "変換")
    (td (italic "Henkan"))
    (td
      (bold "Space")
      " - For these three keys, I have no idea what to map them to.. perhaps I'll do something later but I don't know for now. It also helps with me not missing space as it's a bit smaller now"))
  (tr
    (td "前候補")
    (td (italic "Mae Koho"))
    (td (bold "Space")))
  (tr
    (td "カタカナ/ひらがな/ローマ字")
    (td (italic "Hiragana/Katakana/Romaji"))
    (td (bold "Space"))))

(p
  "I think the Japanese input layout is actually very good for programming but I'm "
  "still getting used to it. Some changes I like are:")

(ul
  (li
    "Colon and semi-colon are now separate--I don't have to press Shift when doing "
    "something on Vim")
  (li
    (bold "@")
    " also doesn't need a shift modifier--Emails, passwords and Vim macros are "
    "even easier")
  (li
    (bold "\"")
    " is on 2! I don't normally use a British keyboard layout but when I do, the "
    "one thing I appreciate is the placement of double-quotation marks on 2."))

(p "Some things I don't like:")

(ul
  (li
    "Underscore, one of the most important keys, is hidden far away next to shift! "
    "I might just remap this to where "
    (italic "Hiragana/Katakana/Romaji")
    " is..")
  (li
    "I think the SpaceBar is also too small (though I might just need some time to "
    "adjust my hand there)")
  (li
    "Single quotation mark on Shift-7. It seems kinda pointless and maybe even a "
    "bit less natural when writing articles like this."))

(p
  "These are some changes that I don't like being an English speaker, I presume "
  "that Japanese speakers don't have some of these problems.")

(image "/Images/MyHHKBExperience/JapaneseKeyboard.png"
  alt: "Japanese keyboard layout")

(h3 "Day Two: 08/08/2026")

(p
  "Today I'm quite busy but I have made a few changes. Firstly, I would like to "
  "mention that I don't like the "
  (code "+")
  " placement on the Japanese layout. I would rather "
  (code "+=")
  " and "
  (code "-_")
  " be under next to each other as they are common keys when programming.")

(p
  "And because I had such difficulties with getting to underscore, I decided to "
  "remap the Hiragana/Katatakana/Romaji key to underscore. It feels so much better "
  "than having to reach to next to shift!")

(p
  "I also had the delight of being able to play Minecraft with this keyboard "
  "today. I can't really say much, other than it felt fine for gaming and didn't "
  "get in the way. I also didn't have any "
  (link "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Key_rollover" "key rollover")
  " which is a plus.")

(h3 "Day Seven: 14/08/2026")

(p
  "It seems I made "
  (italic "three")
  " logs, not two; I didn't feel the need to log the previous days or! Anyways, "
  "here is my conclusion:")

(p
  "Overall I've really enjoyed using this keyboard; despite being membrane, it has "
  "the perfect tactility, I prefer the layout and it's much nicer than those 104 "
  "key keboards. For ~£15 I think it's definately worth it and I hope to use this "
  "for years on.")
